          "id": "verdict-voucher-wallet",
          "title": "The voucher wallet and its auto-invalidation are NATIVE WITH CONFIGURATION, but the engine issues a code string and no QR, and the member-token route to the wallet is deprecated",
          "summary": "VERDICT: native with configuration for expiry and invalidation; integration-layer work for the QR and for member-scoped access. [confidence: strong-signal] The issued-voucher model is richer than the brief assumes. `components.schemas.issuedReward.issuedCoupon` carries `code`, `value`, `valueType` (`money | percentage`), `activeFrom`, `activeTo` and `usedAt` — so per-voucher expiry (BR-P1-016) and a used-at timestamp are both first-class. Expiry is settable per issuance, not just per reward type: the buy bodies `StaticCoupon`, `DynamicCoupon` and `ConversionCoupon` all accept `dateValid`, which satisfies BR-P1-016's 'configurable per reward type' and then some. Invalidation is a supported operation — `POST /api/{storeCode}/member/{member}/reward/redeem` ('Mark coupon as used'), reversible via `.../reward/reissue` ('Mark coupon as unused') — and two webhooks watch the lifecycle: `RewardRedemptionStatusChanged` and `CouponWillExpire`. THREE GAPS, none fatal, all PALO IT's. (a) No QR. The engine returns `issuedCoupon.code` as a string; choosing a symbology, rendering it, and making it legible at a till under bad lighting is member-surface work (brief guiding principle 1, feature f1/f6). Small, but it is not 'native'. (b) The member-token wallet read is deprecated: `GET /api/{storeCode}/member/reward/bought` carries `deprecated: true`. The live alternative, `GET /api/{storeCode}/redemption?customerId=…`, is Integration-labelled but member-agnostic, so the integration layer must broker it and enforce the member's own scope itself. (c) `/redemption`'s 20-odd filters cover `status`, `redemptionDate` and `cancelledAt` but include neither `usedAt` nor `activeTo` — so 'show me my unused, unexpired vouchers', the single most common voucher-wallet query, is a client-side filter over a paged list rather than a server-side one.",
