          "id": "test-t10-parking-cap",
          "title": "T10 — Test whether a wallet-type per-member monthly limit can carry the parking entitlement cap, which nobody has yet asked the engine to do",
          "summary": "OPPORTUNISTIC — outside RA-05's five behaviours, but cheap once the tenant is up and it closes an open design question. [confidence: hypothesis] `WalletTypeLimit.pointsPerMember` accepts a `value` plus an `interval` of `calendarMonths`, which is structurally exactly the parking entitlement's 'capped monthly by tier' (BR-P1-025, feature f8, problem signal s6). CALL: create a second wallet type with `pointsPerMember: { value: 2, interval: { type: calendarMonths, value: 1 } }`, grant against it repeatedly, and observe what happens at and past the cap. LOOK FOR: whether the limit is enforced or advisory; whether the remaining allowance is readable — `components.schemas.Wallet` exposes `unitsLimitUsed` and `unitsLimitRemaining`, which is precisely the number f8 needs to show a member; whether the limit can differ by tier, which BR-P1-025 requires (Tier 1: 1 hour, Tier 2: 2 hours) and a wallet-type-level limit may not support. IF IT WORKS: the parking entitlement gets a real engine-backed counter instead of a bespoke one, and s6's 'how the monthly cap is tracked and shown' is largely answered. Note this does not touch the physical coupon problem, which remains an operations question for RA-04.",
