        {
          "id": "mock-no-webhooks-no-returns",
          "title": "The mock has no webhook subscription surface and no return-transaction handling, so neither the notification contract nor the refund path can be exercised locally at all",
          "summary": "⚠️ DIVERGENCE — an absence rather than a conflict, but the most consequential one for planning. [confidence: strong-signal] Across the mock's ~40 routes there is no `/webhook/subscription`, no `/webhook/event`, no outbound delivery, and no HMAC signing; and while `POST /api/:storeCode/transaction` accepts `documentType: 'return'` and stores it, nothing acts on it — there is no campaign engine, no `cancel_transaction_effects`, and no points reversal. The two Phase 1 mechanics most likely to damage member trust (BR-P1-011 expiry notification and BR-P1-012 refund reversal) are therefore untestable in the local environment. Every claim this desk pass makes about them rests on the specification and the vendor's public documentation alone, and T4 and T5 are the only way to close them.",
