      "description": "Findings that conflict with, or materially change, entries already in the knowledge base. Logged here for the human to action; per the task brief this agent has not edited 02-research-plan.md or raid.gen-e2.raid.",
      "insights": [
        {
          "id": "contradiction-r008-partially-refuted",
          "title": "RAID R008 is half confirmed and half refuted — the engine models wallets and webhooks richly, but the two behaviours R008 singled out are the two that genuinely have no mechanism",
          "summary": "⚠️ CONTRADICTION with RAID R008. [confidence: strong-signal] R008 states that 'wallets, segments, challenges, achievements, custom fields, webhooks and referrals are not modelled' and infers from that that member-facing needs 'may not be expressible in the engine as configured'. The first clause is true of the MOCK and R008 says so; but the inference to the ENGINE does not hold. The vendored spec shows wallets as a first-class configurable type with expiry strategies and per-member limits, 31 HMAC-signed webhook events, a full segment engine with recency conditions, and custom fields throughout. The engine is substantially richer than R008's framing implies, and several member-facing needs are cheaper than feared — voucher expiry and auto-invalidation above all. BUT R008's two named examples land: expiry-cohort visibility is real only through a deprecated route, and multi-redemption (BR-P1-017) has no mechanism at all. RECOMMENDED ACTION FOR THE HUMAN: do not close R008. Narrow it. Its likelihood on the general claim should fall; its impact on the two specific behaviours should hold or rise, and BR-P1-017 deserves its own entry rather than sharing one.",
          "references": [
            {
              "id": "contra-ref-1",
              "sourceId": "RAID",
              "filePath": "gen-e2/discover/customer-app/raid.gen-e2.raid",
              "range": { "start": { "line": 110, "character": 0 }, "end": { "line": 122, "character": 0 } },
              "note": "R008 as written. The mitigation it proposes is exactly RA-05, and this desk pass is the part of that mitigation that could be done without instance access.",
              "excerpt": "\"Member-facing needs such as expiry-cohort visibility (which points lapse when) and stacking multiple vouchers in one transaction (BR-P1-017) may not be expressible in the engine as configured.\""
