              "excerpt": "\"Trigger: access to a real Open Loyalty instance, not the in-repo mock (RAID D005)\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "caveat-spec-provenance",
          "title": "The vendored specification's version field is empty and its provenance is unverified, so it may not match the tenant NTUC Club is given",
          "summary": "[confidence: strong-signal for the observation; hypothesis for the risk] `info.version` in spec/openloyalty-openapi.json is an empty string, and the file's only server entry is `http://openloyalty.localhost`. There is no way to tell from the document which Open Loyalty release it describes, and the repository committed it once with no update history. If the tenant provisioned for NTUC Club runs a different release, endpoints could be present, absent, differently deprecated, or differently scoped. T5's diff of `GET /webhook/event` against the spec's 31 events is the cheapest available check on this, which is another reason to run it early. The expert-interview half of RA-05 should also ask Open Loyalty directly which release the tenant will run and where the versioned specification for it lives.",
          "references": [
            {
              "id": "caveat-ref-2",
              "sourceId": "SPEC",
