              "range": { "start": { "line": 0, "character": 0 }, "end": { "line": 0, "character": 0 } },
              "note": "Spec blocks info and servers. An empty version on a 1.4MB vendored contract is a provenance gap worth logging in RAID.",
              "excerpt": "\"version\": \"\" … \"servers\": [{\"url\": \"http://openloyalty.localhost\"}]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "caveat-expert-interview-half",
          "title": "RA-05's expert-interview half has not been run either, and four questions in this pass are better answered by a person than by a test",
          "summary": "[confidence: assumption] RA-05 is specified as 'expert interview + technical spike'. This desk pass substitutes for neither. Four questions would be answered faster and more reliably by Open Loyalty than by experiment: (1) what replaces `GET /member/{member}/status`, and when is the deprecated route removed; (2) what is the documented consumption order when units expire, since it governs correctness rather than convenience; (3) is there any supported pattern for grouping multiple coupon redemptions against one sale, or any roadmap item for one; (4) which release will the NTUC Club tenant run and where is its versioned specification. Questions 1 and 3 in particular decide whether E1 and E3 are real scope or avoidable, so the interview should be booked in parallel with instance access rather than after it.",
